<div class="nav-panel">
<p>
Next: <a href="rm-invocation.html" accesskey="n" rel="next"><code class="command">rm</code>: Remove files or directories</a>, Previous: <a href="install-invocation.html" accesskey="p" rel="prev"><code class="command">install</code>: Copy files and set attributes</a>, Up: <a href="Basic-operations.html" accesskey="u" rel="up">Basic operations</a> &nbsp; [<a href="index.html#SEC_Contents" title="Table of contents" rel="contents">Contents</a>][<a href="Concept-index.html" title="Index" rel="index">Index</a>]</p>
</div>
<hr>
<h3 class="section" id="mv_003a-Move-_0028rename_0029-files"><span>11.4 <code class="command">mv</code>: Move (rename) files<a class="copiable-link" href="#mv_003a-Move-_0028rename_0029-files"> &para;</a></span></h3>

<a class="index-entry-id" id="index-mv"></a>

<p><code class="command">mv</code> moves or renames files (or directories).  Synopses:
</p>
<div class="example">
<pre class="example-preformatted">mv [<var class="var">option</var>]... [-T] <var class="var">source</var> <var class="var">dest</var>
mv [<var class="var">option</var>]... <var class="var">source</var>... <var class="var">directory</var>
mv [<var class="var">option</var>]... -t <var class="var">directory</var> <var class="var">source</var>...
</pre></div>

<ul class="itemize mark-bullet">
<li>If two file names are given, <code class="command">mv</code> moves the first file to the
second.

</li><li>If the <samp class="option">--target-directory</samp> (<samp class="option">-t</samp>) option is given, or
failing that if the last file is a directory and the
<samp class="option">--no-target-directory</samp> (<samp class="option">-T</samp>) option is not given,
<code class="command">mv</code> moves each <var class="var">source</var> file to the specified
directory, using the <var class="var">source</var>s&rsquo; names.
</li></ul>

<p>To move a file, <code class="command">mv</code> ordinarily simply renames it.
However, if renaming does not work because the destination&rsquo;s file
system differs, <code class="command">mv</code> falls back on copying as if by <code class="code">cp -a</code>,
then (assuming the copy succeeded) it removes the original.
If the copy fails, then <code class="command">mv</code> removes any partially created
copy in the destination.  If you were to copy three directories from
one file system to another and the copy of the first
directory succeeded, but the second didn&rsquo;t, the first would be left on
the destination file system and the second and third would be left on the
original file system.
</p>
<a class="index-entry-id" id="index-extended-attributes_002c-xattr-1"></a>
<p><code class="command">mv</code> always tries to copy extended attributes (xattr), which may
include SELinux context, ACLs or Capabilities.
Upon failure all warnings are emitted, but do not modify the exit
status.
</p>
<a class="index-entry-id" id="index-prompting_002c-and-mv"></a>
<p>If a destination file exists but is normally unwritable, standard input
is a terminal, and the <samp class="option">-f</samp> or <samp class="option">--force</samp> option is not given,
<code class="command">mv</code> prompts the user for whether to replace the file.  (You might
own the file, or have write permission on its directory.)  If the
response is not affirmative, the file is skipped.
</p>
<p>Avoid specifying a source name with a trailing slash,
when it might be a symlink to a directory.
Otherwise, <code class="command">mv</code> may do something very surprising, since
its behavior depends on the underlying rename system call.
On a system with a modern Linux-based kernel, it fails with
<code class="code">errno=ENOTDIR</code>.
However, on other systems (at least FreeBSD 6.1 and Solaris 10) it silently
renames not the symlink but rather the directory referenced by the symlink.
See <a class="xref" href="Trailing-slashes.html">Trailing slashes</a>.
</p>
<p>The <code class="command">mv</code> command replaces destination directories only if they
are empty.  Conflicting populated directories are skipped with a diagnostic.
</p>
<p>The program accepts the following options.  Also see <a class="ref" href="Common-options.html">Common options</a>.
</p>
<dl class="table">
<dd>
<a class="anchor" id="mv-b"></a></dd>
<dt><a class="index-entry-id" id="index-VERSION_005fCONTROL-3"></a>
<a class="index-entry-id" id="index-backups_002c-making-3"></a>
<a id="index-_002d_002dbackup-3"></a><span>&lsquo;<samp class="samp">-b</samp>&rsquo;<a class="copiable-link" href="#index-_002d_002dbackup-3"> &para;</a></span></dt>
<dd><a class="index-entry-id" id="index-_002db-16"></a>
<a class="anchor" id="mv--backup"></a></dd>
<dt>&lsquo;<samp class="samp">--backup[=<var class="var">method</var>]</samp>&rsquo;</dt>
<dd><p>See <a class="xref" href="Backup-options.html">Backup options</a>.
Make a backup of each file that would otherwise be overwritten or removed.
</p>
<a class="anchor" id="mv--debug"></a></dd>
<dt><a class="index-entry-id" id="index-debugging_002c-copying-2"></a>
<a id="index-_002d_002ddebug-6"></a><span>&lsquo;<samp class="samp">--debug</samp>&rsquo;<a class="copiable-link" href="#index-_002d_002ddebug-6"> &para;</a></span></dt>
<dd><p>Print extra information to standard output, explaining how files are copied.
This option implies the <samp class="option">--verbose</samp> option.
</p>
<a class="anchor" id="mv-f"></a></dd>
<dt><a class="index-entry-id" id="index-prompts_002c-omitting-1"></a>
<a id="index-_002d_002dforce-1"></a><span>&lsquo;<samp class="samp">-f</samp>&rsquo;<a class="copiable-link" href="#index-_002d_002dforce-1"> &para;</a></span></dt>
<dd><a class="index-entry-id" id="index-_002df-11"></a>
<a class="anchor" id="mv--force"></a></dd>
<dt>&lsquo;<samp class="samp">--force</samp>&rsquo;</dt>
<dd><p>Do not prompt the user before replacing a destination file.
If you specify more than one of the <samp class="option">-i</samp>, <samp class="option">-f</samp>, <samp class="option">-n</samp>
options, only the final one takes effect.
</p>
<a class="anchor" id="mv-i"></a></dd>
<dt><a class="index-entry-id" id="index-prompts_002c-forcing"></a>
<a id="index-_002d_002dinteractive-1"></a><span>&lsquo;<samp class="samp">-i</samp>&rsquo;<a class="copiable-link" href="#index-_002d_002dinteractive-1"> &para;</a></span></dt>
<dd><a class="index-entry-id" id="index-_002di-12"></a>
<a class="anchor" id="mv--interactive"></a></dd>
<dt>&lsquo;<samp class="samp">--interactive</samp>&rsquo;</dt>
<dd><p>Prompt whether to overwrite each existing destination file, regardless
of its permissions, and fail if the response is not affirmative.
If you specify more than one of the <samp class="option">-i</samp>, <samp class="option">-f</samp>, <samp class="option">-n</samp>
options, only the final one takes effect.
</p>
<a class="anchor" id="mv-n"></a></dd>
<dt><a class="index-entry-id" id="index-prompts_002c-omitting-2"></a>
<a id="index-_002d_002dno_002dclobber-1"></a><span>&lsquo;<samp class="samp">-n</samp>&rsquo;<a class="copiable-link" href="#index-_002d_002dno_002dclobber-1"> &para;</a></span></dt>
<dd><a class="index-entry-id" id="index-_002dn-12"></a>
<a class="anchor" id="mv--no-clobber"></a></dd>
<dt>&lsquo;<samp class="samp">--no-clobber</samp>&rsquo;</dt>
<dd><p>Do not overwrite an existing file; silently skip instead.
If you specify more than one of the <samp class="option">-i</samp>, <samp class="option">-f</samp>, <samp class="option">-n</samp>
options, only the final one takes effect.
This option is mutually exclusive with <samp class="option">-b</samp> or <samp class="option">--backup</samp> option.
This option is deprecated due to having a different exit status from
other platforms.  See also the <samp class="option">--update</samp> option which will
give more control over how to deal with existing files in the destination,
and over the exit status in particular.
</p>
<a class="anchor" id="mv--no-copy"></a></dd>
<dt><a class="index-entry-id" id="index-renaming-files-without-copying-them"></a>
<a id="index-_002d_002dno_002dcopy"></a><span>&lsquo;<samp class="samp">--no-copy</samp>&rsquo;<a class="copiable-link" href="#index-_002d_002dno_002dcopy"> &para;</a></span></dt>
<dd><p>If a file cannot be renamed because the destination file system differs,
fail with a diagnostic instead of copying and then removing the file.
</p>
<a class="anchor" id="mv--exchange"></a></dd>
<dt><a id="index-_002d_002dexchange"></a><span>&lsquo;<samp class="samp">--exchange</samp>&rsquo;<a class="copiable-link" href="#index-_002d_002dexchange"> &para;</a></span></dt>
<dd><p>Exchange source and destination instead of renaming source to destination.
Both files must exist; they need not be the same type.
This exchanges all data and metadata.
</p>
<p>This option can be used to replace one directory with another.
When used this way, it should be combined with
<code class="code">--no-target-directory</code> (<samp class="option">-T</samp>)
to avoid confusion about the destination location.
For example, you might use &lsquo;<samp class="samp">mv -T --exchange <var class="var">d1</var> <var class="var">d2</var></samp>&rsquo;
to exchange two directories <var class="var">d1</var> and <var class="var">d2</var>.
</p>
<p>Exchanges are atomic if the source and destination are both in a
single file system that supports atomic exchange.
Non-atomic exchanges are not yet supported.
</p>
<p>If the source and destination might not be on the same file system,
using <code class="code">--no-copy</code> will prevent future versions of <code class="command">mv</code>
from implementing the exchange by copying.
</p>
<a class="anchor" id="mv-u"></a></dd>
<dt><a class="index-entry-id" id="index-newer-files_002c-moving-only"></a>
<a id="index-_002d_002dupdate-1"></a><span>&lsquo;<samp class="samp">-u</samp>&rsquo;<a class="copiable-link" href="#index-_002d_002dupdate-1"> &para;</a></span></dt>
<dd><a class="index-entry-id" id="index-_002du-7"></a>
<a class="anchor" id="mv--update"></a></dd>
<dt>&lsquo;<samp class="samp">--update[=<var class="var">which</var>]</samp>&rsquo;</dt>
<dd><p>Do not move a non-directory that has an existing destination with the
same or newer modification timestamp;
instead, silently skip the file without failing.
If the move is across file system boundaries, the comparison is to the
source timestamp truncated to the resolutions of the destination file
system and of the system calls used to update timestamps; this avoids
duplicate work if several &lsquo;<samp class="samp">mv -u</samp>&rsquo; commands are executed with the
same source and destination.
This option is ignored if the <samp class="option">-n</samp> or <samp class="option">--no-clobber</samp>
option is also specified.
</p>
<p><var class="var">which</var> gives more control over which existing files in the
destination are replaced, and its value can be one of the following:
</p>
<dl class="table">
<dt>&lsquo;<samp class="samp">all</samp>&rsquo;</dt>
<dd><p>This is the default operation when an <samp class="option">--update</samp> option is not specified,
and results in all existing files in the destination being replaced.
</p>
</dd>
<dt>&lsquo;<samp class="samp">none</samp>&rsquo;</dt>
<dd><p>This is like the deprecated <samp class="option">--no-clobber</samp> option, where no files in the
destination are replaced, and also skipping a file does not induce a failure.
</p>
</dd>
<dt>&lsquo;<samp class="samp">none-fail</samp>&rsquo;</dt>
<dd><p>This is similar to &lsquo;<samp class="samp">none</samp>&rsquo;, in that no files in the destination
are replaced, but any skipped files are diagnosed and induce a failure.
</p>
</dd>
<dt>&lsquo;<samp class="samp">older</samp>&rsquo;</dt>
<dd><p>This is the default operation when <samp class="option">--update</samp> is specified, and results
in files being replaced if they&rsquo;re older than the corresponding source file.
</p></dd>
</dl>

<a class="anchor" id="mv-v"></a></dd>
<dt><a id="index-_002d_002dverbose-5"></a><span>&lsquo;<samp class="samp">-v</samp>&rsquo;<a class="copiable-link" href="#index-_002d_002dverbose-5"> &para;</a></span></dt>
<dd><a class="index-entry-id" id="index-_002dv-10"></a>
<a class="anchor" id="mv--verbose"></a></dd>
<dt>&lsquo;<samp class="samp">--verbose</samp>&rsquo;</dt>
<dd><p>Print the name of each file before moving it.
</p>
<a class="anchor" id="mv--strip-trailing-slashes"></a></dd>
<dt><a class="index-entry-id" id="index-stripping-trailing-slashes-1"></a>
<a id="index-_002d_002dstrip_002dtrailing_002dslashes-1"></a><span>&lsquo;<samp class="samp">--strip-trailing-slashes</samp>&rsquo;<a class="copiable-link" href="#index-_002d_002dstrip_002dtrailing_002dslashes-1"> &para;</a></span></dt>
<dd><p>Remove any trailing slashes from each <var class="var">source</var> argument.
See <a class="xref" href="Trailing-slashes.html">Trailing slashes</a>.
</p>
<a class="anchor" id="mv-S"></a></dd>
<dt><a id="index-_002d_002dsuffix-3"></a><span>&lsquo;<samp class="samp">-S&nbsp;<!-- /@w --><var class="var">suffix</var></samp>&rsquo;<a class="copiable-link" href="#index-_002d_002dsuffix-3"> &para;</a></span></dt>
<dd><a class="index-entry-id" id="index-_002dS-8"></a>
<a class="anchor" id="mv--suffix"></a></dd>
<dt>&lsquo;<samp class="samp">--suffix=<var class="var">suffix</var></samp>&rsquo;</dt>
<dd><p>Append <var class="var">suffix</var> to each backup file made with <samp class="option">-b</samp>.
See <a class="xref" href="Backup-options.html">Backup options</a>.
</p>
<a class="anchor" id="mv-t"></a></dd>
<dt><a class="index-entry-id" id="index-target-directory-7"></a>
<a class="index-entry-id" id="index-destination-directory-6"></a>
<a id="index-_002d_002dtarget_002ddirectory-3"></a><span>&lsquo;<samp class="samp">-t&nbsp;<!-- /@w --><var class="var">directory</var></samp>&rsquo;<a class="copiable-link" href="#index-_002d_002dtarget_002ddirectory-3"> &para;</a></span></dt>
<dd><a class="index-entry-id" id="index-_002dt-15"></a>
<a class="anchor" id="mv--target-directory"></a></dd>
<dt>&lsquo;<samp class="samp">--target-directory=<var class="var">directory</var></samp>&rsquo;</dt>
<dd><p>Specify the destination <var class="var">directory</var>.
See <a class="xref" href="Target-directory.html">Target directory</a>.
</p>
<a class="anchor" id="mv-T"></a></dd>
<dt><a class="index-entry-id" id="index-target-directory-8"></a>
<a class="index-entry-id" id="index-destination-directory-7"></a>
<a id="index-_002d_002dno_002dtarget_002ddirectory-3"></a><span>&lsquo;<samp class="samp">-T</samp>&rsquo;<a class="copiable-link" href="#index-_002d_002dno_002dtarget_002ddirectory-3"> &para;</a></span></dt>
<dd><a class="index-entry-id" id="index-_002dT-7"></a>
<a class="anchor" id="mv--no-target-directory"></a></dd>
<dt>&lsquo;<samp class="samp">--no-target-directory</samp>&rsquo;</dt>
<dd><p>Do not treat the last operand specially when it is a directory or a
symbolic link to a directory.  See <a class="xref" href="Target-directory.html">Target directory</a>.
</p>
<a class="anchor" id="mv-Z"></a></dd>
<dt><a class="index-entry-id" id="index-SELinux_002c-restoring-security-context"></a>
<a class="index-entry-id" id="index-security-context-4"></a>
<a id="index-_002d_002dcontext-3"></a><span>&lsquo;<samp class="samp">-Z</samp>&rsquo;<a class="copiable-link" href="#index-_002d_002dcontext-3"> &para;</a></span></dt>
<dd><a class="index-entry-id" id="index-_002dZ-3"></a>
<a class="anchor" id="mv--context"></a></dd>
<dt>&lsquo;<samp class="samp">--context</samp>&rsquo;</dt>
<dd><p>This option functions similarly to the <code class="command">restorecon</code> command,
by adjusting the SELinux security context according
to the system default type for destination files and each created directory.
</p>
</dd>
</dl>

<p>An exit status of zero indicates success,
and a nonzero value indicates failure.
</p>

</div>
